  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sounder Ganesh vs The District Revenue Officer on 23 August, 2024 Author: R.Subramanian Bench: R.Subramanian W.P.(MD)Nos.19591 and 21195 of Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 23.08.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice R.Subramanian and The Honourable Mrs.Justice L.Victoria Gowri W.P.(MD)Nos.19591 and 21195 of 2021 and W.M.P(MD)Nos.16292 and 17774 of 2021 W.P.(MD)No.19591 of 2021 Sounder Ganesh ... Petitioner -vs- The District Revenue Officer (Grievance Redressal Officer), Cum Additional District Executive Magistrate, Virudhunagar District. ... Respondent PRAYER: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of Constitution of India, to issue a Writ of Certiorari to call for the records pertaining to the impug proceedings issued by the respondent vide his proceedings in case No. 53/2020-21 dated 13.08.2021 and quash the same as illegal. For Petitioner : Mr.B.Jameel Arasu For Respondent : Mr.P.T.Thiraviyam, Government Advocate Sounder Ganesh vs The District Revenue Officer on 23 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/16724940/ 1 W.P.(MD)No.21195 of 2021 ____________ https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Page 1 of 5 W.P.(MD)Nos.19591 and 21195 o Sri Ganesh & Co., Represented by its Partner, B.Sudalaimani, S/o.P.Balagurusamy, Having office at, 4B/1-C, New Ramnad Road, Theppakulam Mettu Street, Madurai-625 009. ... Petitioner -vs- 1.Food Safety Officer, Aruppukottai Municipality & Union, Kaariyapatti Union, Virudhunagar District. 2.The Adjudicating Authority, The District Revenue Officer, Virudhunagar District. ... Respondents PRAYER: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of Constitution of India, to issue a Writ of Certiorari to call for the records relating to the impugne order passed by the 2nd respondent in Case No.40/2020-2021 dated 13.08.2021 and quash the same. For Petitioner : Mr.M.Rajaraman For Respondents : Mr.P.T.Thiraviyam, Government Advocate COMMON ORDER [Order of the Court was made by R.SUBRAMANIAN, J.] Though the learned Single Judge had directed transfer of the writ petitions to the Tamil Nadu Food Safety Appellate Tribunal, when the same ____________ https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(MD)Nos.19591 and 21195 of 2021 was placed before one of us (Hon'ble Mr.Justice.R.Subramanian) in the administrative capacity, a Sounder Ganesh vs The District Revenue Officer on 23 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/16724940/",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. The learned counsel for the petitioner in the writ petitions would fairly concede that transfer of a writ petitions filed under Article 226 to a statutory Tribunal may set a bad precedent."
  },
